$C_1=10 \mu \mathrm{ F}, \mathrm{ V}_1=100 \mathrm{ V}, \mathrm{C}_2=\mu \mathrm{F}, \mathrm{ V}_2=0$During sharing of capacitors,
$\begin{aligned}
& \text{ Energy lost, } \Delta U=\frac{1}{2}\left(\frac{C_1 C_2}{C_1+C_2}\right)\left(V_1-V_2\right)^2 \\
& =\frac{1}{2}\left(\frac{10 \times 30}{10+30}\right)(100)^2 \times 10^{-6} \\
& =3.75 \times 10^{-2} \mathrm{ J}
\end{aligned}$

